<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hebei</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hebei is a province of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> surrounding present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> it was an important region for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-smelting">iron production</a> on a large scale. It also lay on the frontier with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> and later fell to the Jin.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hebei.jpg" alt="Hebei" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Whereisthetruthicantfindyou · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fengning_Jing_Bei_meadow.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
